<% content_for :title, "Teacher stocks preview" %>
<%# A design preview, reachable only where the component gallery is - `Rails.env.local?`.

    The proposal: a teacher has no view of a company that has stopped trading. `StockPolicy` already
    records why - "a teacher cannot open /admin/stocks, so it was their only view of the catalogue" - and
    the archived-stocks rule shows an archived company only to a student who holds it. A teacher holds
    nothing, so they get nothing.

    Two shapes are rendered below. Neither is built yet. %>
<div class="mx-auto max-w-5xl">
  <%= admin_breadcrumbs(@breadcrumbs) %>

  <%= render layout: "components/ui/page_header",
             locals: { title: "Teacher stocks preview",
                       description: "Two ways to give a teacher a read-only list of closed companies. " \
                                    "Nothing here is built - this is for choosing between them." } do %><% end %>

  <div class="space-y-6">
    <%= render layout: "components/ui/callout",
               locals: { tone: :info,
                         title: "Recommended: option 1, a second section",
                         body: "The trading floor is already a stack of sections and a teacher's copy of " \
                               "it is already read-only, so this adds a section rather than a mode. " \
                               "Tabs make Archived a peer of Active and hide one to show the other, on " \
                               "a page whose job is what students can buy today." } do %><% end %>

    <section aria-labelledby="opt1">
      <h2 id="opt1" class="text-base font-semibold text-slate-900">Option 1 - a second section, below</h2>
      <p class="mt-1 text-sm text-slate-600">
        What a teacher would find on <code>/stocks</code>. The Held by column is the reason it earns a
        place: it answers which of their students still hold a company that has closed.
      </p>

      <div class="mt-3 rounded-2xl border border-slate-200 bg-slate-50 p-4">
        <p class="mb-3 text-xs font-medium text-slate-600">Rendered as staff - no Buy or Sell anywhere</p>
        <div class="space-y-6">
          <% if @preview_active.any? %>
            <%= render "stocks/stocks_table",
                       title: "Active stocks",
                       description: "Companies your students can buy shares in right now.",
                       stocks: @preview_active %>
          <% end %>
          <% if @preview_archived.any? %>
            <%= render "stocks/stocks_table",
                       title: "Archived stocks",
                       description: "These companies no longer trade here, so nobody can buy them. " \
                                    "They stay listed for 12 months after they close.",
                       stocks: @preview_archived %>
          <% end %>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="mt-4 rounded-lg border border-slate-200 bg-white p-4 text-sm text-slate-700">
        <ul class="list-disc space-y-1 pl-5">
          <li><strong class="font-medium text-slate-900">Costs</strong> vertical space on a page whose
            first job is the active list, and grows with the 12-month window.</li>
          <li><strong class="font-medium text-slate-900">Gives</strong> the answer without a mode switch,
            and matches how a holding student already meets the same rows.</li>
          <li>Students are untouched - the section is staff-only, so nothing changes on their screen.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section aria-labelledby="opt2">
      <h2 id="opt2" class="text-base font-semibold text-slate-900">Option 2 - Active / Archived tabs</h2>
      <p class="mt-1 text-sm text-slate-600">
        The pattern the admin indexes use for the same idea, borrowed onto the trading floor.
      </p>

      <div class="mt-3 rounded-2xl border border-slate-200 bg-slate-50 p-4">
        <p class="mb-3 text-xs font-medium text-slate-600">Mock - the tabs do nothing here</p>
        <nav class="mb-4 flex gap-1" aria-label="Stock state (mock)">
          <span class="rounded-lg bg-white px-3 py-1.5 text-sm font-medium text-slate-900 shadow-sm">Active</span>
          <span class="rounded-lg px-3 py-1.5 text-sm font-medium text-slate-600">Archived</span>
        </nav>
        <% if @preview_active.any? %>
          <%= render "stocks/stocks_table", stocks: @preview_active %>
        <% end %>
      </div>

      <div class="mt-4 rounded-lg border border-slate-200 bg-white p-4 text-sm text-slate-700">
        <ul class="list-disc space-y-1 pl-5">
          <li><strong class="font-medium text-slate-900">Costs</strong> the two lists at once: a teacher
            comparing "is this company still listed" has to switch and come back.</li>
          <li>It puts a control on a student's page that only staff may operate, or a control that
            appears for some roles - both are worse than a section.</li>
          <li><strong class="font-medium text-slate-900">Gives</strong> consistency with the admin
            indexes, which is real but is a consistency with a different kind of page.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section aria-labelledby="opt3">
      <h2 id="opt3" class="text-base font-semibold text-slate-900">What both need</h2>
      <div class="mt-3 rounded-lg border border-slate-200 bg-white p-4 text-sm text-slate-700">
        <ul class="list-disc space-y-1 pl-5">
          <li>A <code>StockPolicy</code> predicate - staff only - so a student&rsquo;s page is unchanged
            and the rule has one home.</li>
          <li>The 12-month window, <code>Stock.archived_recently</code>, so the teacher list and the admin
            list agree about what &ldquo;archived&rdquo; means.</li>
          <li>A test asserting a student still gets nothing, which is the rule that was just settled.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </section>
  </div>
</div>
